/*
Mental trigger

“Bit reversal → mirror bit positions across the center.”

Time complexity

O(32) → constant time

Space complexity

O(1)

Simple intuition

A 32-bit number has fixed positions: 0 … 31

Take the bit at position i

Place it at position 31 − i

Do this for all 32 bits

That’s all reversal means.
*/
class Solution {
    public int reverseBits(int n) {
        int res = 0;
        for(int i=0;i<32;i++){
            int bit = (n>>i) & 1;
            res+= (bit<< (31-i));
        }
        return res;
    }
}
